      "name": null,
      "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(x-4)^{2}=-24(y+5)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =4(-6)(y+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-6.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=4$ and $k=-5.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(4,-5).$",
